{
  "description": "A Foxhound Client starts the crawl `nightly` and closes it, which aborts it, then starts it again by its Run ID: the engine leases `nightly`'s seed, whose handler closes the first Run value a second time and enqueues under `nightly`, then the page it enqueued, whose handler enqueues again; each handler call is answered `{}`. Closing the Connection then aborts the Run started again.",
